WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.970
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.240 --> 00:02.000
Dr. Pun.

3
00:03.960 --> 00:05.120
I’m Monsieur.

4
00:06.960 --> 00:11.600
Now that we’ve revealed our real identities, how about we start going out?

5
00:15.440 --> 00:18.000
Be careful with your mixed signals.

6
00:18.600 --> 00:20.320
Someone else might get to him first.

7
00:21.640 --> 00:22.120
Moth.

8
00:23.560 --> 00:26.080
Why don’t we just get together?

9
02:12.440 --> 02:13.200
What did you say?

10
02:18.400 --> 02:18.760
Uh…

11
02:20.600 --> 02:21.600
Just pretend you didn’t hear that.

12
02:24.920 --> 02:25.480
Moth.

13
02:46.079 --> 02:46.600
Mes.

14
02:54.680 --> 02:55.400
How have you been?

15
02:56.120 --> 02:56.840
Doing well?

16
02:58.800 --> 02:59.400
I am.

17
03:00.680 --> 03:01.720
It’s been a long time.

18
03:18.120 --> 03:22.160
Ah, that’s Dean.

19
03:24.400 --> 03:25.240
My friend.

20
03:30.800 --> 03:31.240
Ah.

21
03:32.680 --> 03:33.200
Hi.

22
03:34.200 --> 03:35.160
I’m Mes, his senior.

23
03:35.880 --> 03:36.400
Senior?

24
03:42.040 --> 03:43.040
Let me know when you get home.

25
03:47.360 --> 03:49.800
Should we head upstairs?

26
03:52.480 --> 03:53.040
Sure.

27
04:40.080 --> 04:40.600
Here you go.

28
04:44.720 --> 04:47.560
It’s been with me for so long. I thought you didn’t want it back.

29
04:48.640 --> 04:49.360
Of course I do.

30
04:50.200 --> 04:53.200
Back in uni, I had to save up for a month to buy this.

31
04:54.880 --> 04:57.960
When you had it, did you ever read it?

32
05:01.480 --> 05:02.320
Not really.

33
05:04.520 --> 05:06.120
I usually use different references.

34
05:16.800 --> 05:17.840
So how did you get here?

35
05:18.760 --> 05:19.640
Did you drive?

36
05:21.280 --> 05:22.080
I took a cab.

37
05:23.520 --> 05:24.160
Why?

38
05:25.200 --> 05:29.080
Now that you gave it back, you’re trying to get rid of me already?

39
05:31.080 --> 05:32.080
Nonsense, Mes.

40
05:32.720 --> 05:33.760
Who would ever want to get rid of you?

41
05:37.400 --> 05:38.400
Make yourself at home.

42
05:41.080 --> 05:42.200
You’re still the same, Moth.

43
05:47.840 --> 05:48.560
How are you doing?

44
05:49.520 --> 05:51.120
I see you post a lot of work pieces on IG.

45
05:51.880 --> 05:53.000
Do you even have time to rest?

46
05:57.880 --> 05:58.920
Work’s been pretty hectic lately.

47
06:00.080 --> 06:01.200
The faster I get it done, the faster I get paid.

48
06:03.640 --> 06:04.960
You should make time to travel.

49
06:05.800 --> 06:07.680
When you decide to go to New York, let me know.

50
06:08.080 --> 06:08.800
I’ll show you around.

51
06:10.480 --> 06:15.080
So, you’re back this time. Are you staying long?

52
06:16.280 --> 06:18.720
Mhm, I think I’ll be here for a while.

53
06:19.360 --> 06:21.200
A gallery asked me to showcase my work.

54
06:21.440 --> 06:22.960
They’re also holding a charity auction.

55
06:24.040 --> 06:25.080
Hey, the exhibition opens the day after tomorrow.

56
06:28.880 --> 06:29.760
Moth, you should come.

57
06:30.840 --> 06:31.760
I want you to come.

58
06:55.680 --> 06:57.080
[WHAT ARE YOU DOING?]

59
07:23.920 --> 07:33.440
[CONGRATS, MES! WE’RE SO PROUD OF YOU.]

60
08:32.400 --> 08:33.400
You got here fast.

61
08:34.760 --> 08:36.080
Didn’t we say 10 a.m.?

62
08:37.720 --> 08:39.360
I got here at eight to queue up.

63
08:39.559 --> 08:40.720
Isn’t that a little early?

64
08:41.200 --> 08:48.240
You’re only free in the morning because you have to be at the clinic at noon.

65
08:49.040 --> 08:51.800
And there aren’t many good breakfast places around here.

66
08:52.640 --> 08:56.200
Luckily, I found this place online. The reviews are great.

67
08:56.560 --> 08:58.600
They say the food is really good.

68
08:58.800 --> 09:01.040
But it’s always packed, so I had to come super early.

69
09:06.360 --> 09:07.720
Don’t you like it, Dr. Pun?

70
09:08.920 --> 09:09.440
I do.

71
09:10.880 --> 09:12.200
But it sounds like a hassle for you.

72
09:14.400 --> 09:15.960
No, it’s fine.

73
09:16.840 --> 09:22.680
You’re my first boyfriend,

74
09:24.240 --> 09:30.560
and this is our first time going out as boyfriends,

75
09:31.920 --> 09:33.920
so I wanted to impress you.

76
09:39.280 --> 09:42.280
Oh, did I say “boyfriend” too many times?

77
09:42.760 --> 09:43.520
I’m sorry.

78
09:46.680 --> 09:48.000
You can say it as many times as you want.

79
09:50.880 --> 09:52.040
We really are boyfriends.

80
09:57.560 --> 09:59.840
Thank you for trying to impress me.

81
10:01.680 --> 10:09.040
But if we can, I’d rather we come together.

82
10:12.600 --> 10:15.320
So you’re okay with coming at 5 a.m.?

83
10:17.160 --> 10:18.040
I’m joking.

84
10:18.760 --> 10:21.120
If we have to come at five, we might as well find a new restaurant.

85
10:22.680 --> 10:24.000
Let’s order.

86
11:04.400 --> 11:05.360
Moth’s calling.

87
11:06.200 --> 11:07.040
Can I answer?

88
11:07.840 --> 11:08.960
Of course.

89
11:09.400 --> 11:09.920
Why not?

90
11:15.000 --> 11:15.680
Ah.

91
11:17.840 --> 11:19.200
You don’t have to worry about me.

92
11:19.640 --> 11:21.560
You and Moth are friends.

93
11:27.240 --> 11:28.680
Hello. What’s up?

94
11:29.280 --> 11:30.360
(Can we meet before noon?)

95
11:31.120 --> 11:31.920
(I’ll come see you.)

96
11:40.280 --> 11:41.280
Can we meet another day?

97
11:42.920 --> 11:43.720
I’m with...

98
11:43.720 --> 11:44.680
(Mes is back.)

99
11:49.520 --> 11:52.520
(BUDDY HEAL CLINIC)

100
12:02.640 --> 12:05.360
He went straight to your place after flying back from abroad?

101
12:07.960 --> 12:08.720
Not really.

102
12:10.240 --> 12:11.240
He’s been back for a while.

103
12:12.640 --> 12:13.480
He just…

104
12:14.880 --> 12:16.560
came by to get his book.

105
12:19.840 --> 12:22.400
Why didn’t you just send it with a messenger?

106
12:28.160 --> 12:30.000
I thought I was over him.

107
12:34.120 --> 12:38.600
But then I saw him in person, and I was back to square one.

108
12:42.320 --> 12:43.360
I didn’t know how to act.

109
12:45.200 --> 12:47.040
If I were you, I wouldn’t have met him in the first place.

110
13:03.400 --> 13:03.800
Hey.

111
13:05.040 --> 13:05.880
I’m dating Ten now.

112
13:08.440 --> 13:08.880
Huh?

113
13:10.480 --> 13:14.040
I was going to tell you today, but you told me about Mes first.

114
13:17.680 --> 13:20.000
Then I’m happy for you.

115
13:21.920 --> 13:23.400
When did you decide?

116
13:24.760 --> 13:25.600
Why didn’t I know about this?

117
13:27.560 --> 13:28.160
Yesterday.

118
13:30.080 --> 13:32.240
But I’ve been talking to him for a while.

119
13:33.040 --> 13:36.280
And I wanted to break out of the same cycle.

120
13:42.440 --> 13:45.520
As for you, do whatever you think is right.

121
13:47.120 --> 13:52.240
But if you can, I’d rather not hear about this anymore.

122
14:16.920 --> 14:17.600
I’m sorry, Pun.

123
14:18.120 --> 14:19.000
There’s a bit of a problem.

124
14:20.440 --> 14:21.320
Sorry about what?

125
14:23.080 --> 14:25.360
Hi. Can I be your plus-one today?

126
14:26.720 --> 14:27.560
Be my guest.

127
14:28.560 --> 14:32.120
Hey, Pun, do you know a guy named Mes?

128
14:32.960 --> 14:33.800
You’ve met him?

129
14:34.320 --> 14:36.240
Yeah, big time. At Moth’s place.

130
14:39.520 --> 14:41.400
Mes was Moth’s senior at university,

131
14:43.640 --> 14:44.360
and also…

132
14:46.080 --> 14:47.200
Moth’s first love.

133
14:50.680 --> 14:52.120
Mes was someone Moth looked up to.

134
14:54.240 --> 14:55.520
Moth wanted to be like him.

135
14:57.120 --> 14:59.920
He wanted to stand beside him.

136
15:14.560 --> 15:16.480
Why don’t you try adding some white as a highlight?

137
15:29.480 --> 15:30.280
Thank you, Mes.

138
15:31.400 --> 15:32.840
It feels like I’m always relying on you.

139
15:33.560 --> 15:34.800
You’ll surpass me very soon.

140
15:36.600 --> 15:39.240
One day, you might be the one helping me.

141
15:41.680 --> 15:42.160
You’re exaggerating.

142
15:43.480 --> 15:45.520
Me? Better than you?

143
15:47.520 --> 15:50.600
Moth, don’t ever think you’re ordinary.

144
15:51.160 --> 15:52.000
You know why?

145
15:54.960 --> 15:56.200
Because you paint with your feelings.

146
15:57.280 --> 15:58.520
You don’t care whether it’s right or wrong.

147
15:59.880 --> 16:01.240
Precision and skill can be learned.

148
16:02.280 --> 16:03.720
But feelings are what truly belong to us.

149
16:04.560 --> 16:08.560
If you let your feelings flow and stay true to them,

150
16:12.440 --> 16:20.240
they’ll show through in your work.

151
16:23.200 --> 16:24.200
Promise me, Moth.

152
16:26.280 --> 16:27.960
Don’t ever let that disappear.

153
16:30.800 --> 16:32.360
I’d love to keep seeing it.

154
16:37.440 --> 16:41.480
Well, if you don’t disappear from my life, you’ll get to keep seeing it.

155
16:42.720 --> 16:44.640
Art brought those two together.

156
16:46.160 --> 16:47.680
I wasn’t in the same faculty as Moth,

157
16:48.360 --> 16:51.440
so I don’t know if Mes was simply interested in his work

158
16:52.160 --> 16:54.560
or if, deep down, he felt something more.

159
16:56.360 --> 17:00.520
But hearing Moth talk about Mes every day, I knew one thing for sure.

160
17:01.160 --> 17:03.560
Moth had truly fallen in love with him.

161
17:08.000 --> 17:11.599
Until one day, Moth had a wake-up call.

162
17:18.160 --> 17:20.440
Happy Valentine’s, Mes.

163
17:26.880 --> 17:28.200
I’m not into this kind of thing.

164
17:36.840 --> 17:37.600
Are you?

165
17:43.920 --> 17:44.440
Well…

166
17:47.480 --> 17:48.320
Not really.

167
17:55.840 --> 17:56.920
You know what’s funny?

168
17:57.880 --> 18:00.640
A year later, Mes went abroad to study.

169
18:01.960 --> 18:02.760
He started dating someone

170
18:03.760 --> 18:06.280
and posted new content with his partner every Valentine’s Day.

171
18:07.320 --> 18:10.760
But Moth ended up hating Valentine’s Day instead.

172
18:12.760 --> 18:14.560
Mes’s partner had an impressive profile,

173
18:15.520 --> 18:17.400
so Moth thought he wasn’t good enough.

174
18:20.880 --> 18:23.880
Could anyone really make Moth feel like he wasn’t good enough?

175
18:27.680 --> 18:31.200
Deep down, everyone compares themselves to others.

176
18:32.080 --> 18:33.120
Especially Moth.

177
18:33.840 --> 18:36.840
The guy who never says what he really thinks out loud.

178
18:42.920 --> 18:47.680
If Moth was that heartbroken over him, then why is he still being nice to him?

179
18:50.240 --> 18:53.880
All this time, he’s been mean to everyone who’s tried to hit on him,

180
18:55.640 --> 18:57.600
partly because of the hurt he still carries inside…

181
18:59.240 --> 19:04.120
and partly because he still can’t get over Mes.

182
19:35.760 --> 19:36.360
Hello.

183
19:37.480 --> 19:38.160
(Are you free to talk?)

184
19:41.600 --> 19:42.520
What’s up, Mes?

185
19:44.360 --> 19:49.040
(I opened the book you gave me and found all these notes.)

186
19:49.760 --> 19:52.760
(They brought back memories, so I called.)

187
19:55.520 --> 19:59.480
(I remember you were such a nerd about contemporary and abstract art.)

188
20:09.040 --> 20:10.480
But I forgot all about it now.

189
20:10.680 --> 20:11.680
(Don’t lie.)

190
20:12.280 --> 20:15.080
(You don’t just forget things like that.)

191
20:20.520 --> 20:25.560
(Hey, that photo of the artwork you put in the book, I saw the original.)

192
20:26.040 --> 20:26.680
Really?

193
20:27.080 --> 20:32.040
(Yes. I’m telling you, the actual piece was stunning. It was even better than the photo.)

194
20:41.160 --> 20:42.440
We’re heading somewhere next.

195
20:45.160 --> 20:46.520
You want to come with us?

196
20:48.080 --> 20:51.080
Only asking out of courtesy, though.

197
20:53.040 --> 20:53.480
Ten.

198
20:55.080 --> 20:58.880
Yeah, I know you want some alone time with Pun.

199
21:00.720 --> 21:01.400
I won’t get in your way.

200
21:02.400 --> 21:02.960
Have fun.

201
21:05.640 --> 21:12.240
Hey. I forgot to say something important.

202
21:14.200 --> 21:15.600
I’m really happy for you.

203
21:18.320 --> 21:22.080
You deserve a love this good.

204
21:23.320 --> 21:28.720
And thank you, Pun, for opening your heart to Ten.

205
21:29.560 --> 21:33.400
I believe he can make you happy.

206
21:34.120 --> 21:37.880
I want to make Ten happy, too.

207
21:46.200 --> 21:46.920
We’re off now.

208
21:47.280 --> 21:48.600
Yeah. See you later.

209
22:00.360 --> 22:06.440
[WHAT ARE YOU DOING?]

210
22:33.840 --> 22:35.360
(Hey, I gotta go.)

211
22:35.360 --> 22:37.320
(I’ve got some work to finish.)

212
22:45.920 --> 22:49.760
[20 MISSED CALLS FROM MANIAC]

213
22:54.440 --> 22:55.040
Hello.

214
22:57.200 --> 22:57.760
I saw your missed calls.

215
22:58.560 --> 22:59.560
(I’m downstairs.)

216
22:59.840 --> 23:00.520
(Come down and meet me.)

217
23:04.800 --> 23:05.800
Why was your line busy?

218
23:06.320 --> 23:07.120
Because I was on the phone.

219
23:07.800 --> 23:08.320
Who were you talking to?

220
23:10.320 --> 23:10.920
A senior.

221
23:12.560 --> 23:13.640
You wouldn’t know him.

222
23:13.800 --> 23:14.640
Is he really just a senior?

223
23:15.440 --> 23:16.760
You two talked for an hour.

224
23:17.160 --> 23:19.120
If you’re going to be like this, I don’t want to talk.

225
23:20.160 --> 23:20.560
Wait.

226
23:24.320 --> 23:24.840
Fine.

227
23:27.120 --> 23:27.840
Where are you going tomorrow?

228
23:28.560 --> 23:29.320
Out.

229
23:30.400 --> 23:31.000
I’ve got something to do.

230
23:31.160 --> 23:31.840
With who?

231
23:35.680 --> 23:36.520
I need to deposit a check.

232
23:36.600 --> 23:37.200
And then?

233
23:37.200 --> 23:38.160
Are you spending all day depositing your check?

234
23:38.160 --> 23:39.000
What’s wrong with you?

235
23:39.880 --> 23:40.960
Just say whatever you want to say.

236
23:40.960 --> 23:41.760
Oh, can I?

237
23:44.600 --> 23:47.840
Then crystallize your thoughts and figure out what you really want to say.

238
23:50.320 --> 23:50.760
Wait.

239
23:53.480 --> 23:55.360
Fine. I’ll say it.

240
23:56.800 --> 23:57.680
Let me ask you something.

241
24:03.840 --> 24:04.640
What are we, exactly?

242
24:13.680 --> 24:14.200
I don’t know either.

243
24:36.960 --> 24:37.640
Please, come in.

244
24:38.400 --> 24:39.960
Sorry, my place is a little messy.

245
24:41.240 --> 24:43.080
You can sit right here.

246
24:49.560 --> 24:52.000
We have a guest today, girl.

247
24:52.640 --> 24:54.400
How are you doing, sweetheart?

248
24:57.160 --> 24:57.720
Wow.

249
24:57.960 --> 24:58.800
Let’s have some snacks.

250
24:59.360 --> 25:00.800
You’ve got your yum-yum.

251
25:03.560 --> 25:04.600
Would you like to hold her?

252
25:05.160 --> 25:05.800
Whoa.

253
25:06.280 --> 25:07.520
She looks so much healthier.

254
25:29.720 --> 25:33.800
Dr. Pun, you can play with Mademoiselle for now.

255
25:34.640 --> 25:37.640
I need to upload and submit my work file.

256
25:38.520 --> 25:39.240
It won’t take long.

257
25:39.920 --> 25:40.480
Of course.

258
25:40.840 --> 25:41.680
Take your time.

259
25:42.400 --> 25:43.480
I’ll stay here with her.

260
25:44.480 --> 25:45.160
All right, then.

261
25:53.760 --> 25:57.680
Does your papa even know what I’m doing at his house?

262
26:03.320 --> 26:03.920
Shit!

263
26:08.480 --> 26:10.000
I think the transformer outside just blew.

264
26:15.800 --> 26:16.840
The technician hasn’t come to fix it yet.

265
26:18.120 --> 26:19.120
It should take a while.

266
26:20.640 --> 26:23.040
Dr. Pun, would you rather leave now?

267
26:23.360 --> 26:24.080
No, it’s okay.

268
26:25.440 --> 26:26.800
I’d rather stay and keep you company.

269
26:30.240 --> 26:30.960
Are you sure?

270
26:44.040 --> 26:44.840
I’m sorry.

271
26:45.960 --> 26:47.200
Did I disappoint you?

272
26:49.320 --> 26:51.200
Why would you think that?

273
26:54.120 --> 27:01.240
Well, I’m afraid I’m making you feel like I’m not what you expected.

274
27:04.760 --> 27:05.360
No.

275
27:07.440 --> 27:09.280
Everyone has their own strengths and weaknesses.

276
27:10.680 --> 27:13.760
To me, you’re a really good listener.

277
27:19.120 --> 27:19.760
Then…

278
27:22.560 --> 27:24.640
I’ll just listen to you talk.

279
27:26.800 --> 27:27.640
What should I talk about?

280
27:29.000 --> 27:32.840
I think my life is pretty boring.

281
27:34.960 --> 27:40.680
How about telling me things that help me get to know you better?

282
27:42.480 --> 27:43.320
Um…

283
27:44.520 --> 27:46.200
You already know my name.

284
27:46.840 --> 27:50.160
My date of birth? I was born on October 15.

285
27:51.360 --> 27:52.280
Bachelor’s degree in veterinary medicine.

286
27:53.240 --> 27:56.040
I only have one close friend. That’s Moth.

287
28:05.520 --> 28:11.600
Mes being back this time doesn’t just affect Dean and Moth.

288
28:13.440 --> 28:14.280
You’re right.

289
28:15.880 --> 28:18.600
It affects me, too.

290
28:20.440 --> 28:22.000
I have to keep consoling Dean.

291
28:30.880 --> 28:32.400
It reminds me of the past,

292
28:36.400 --> 28:37.800
when I secretly had a crush on Moth.

293
28:40.560 --> 28:41.960
Moth secretly had a crush on Mes.

294
28:43.840 --> 28:47.440
We just kept going around in circles, endlessly.

295
29:04.720 --> 29:07.000
But I never want to go back to that same cycle again.

296
29:11.400 --> 29:12.520
Because I have you now.

297
29:20.880 --> 29:23.600
I really want to open a new book and start reading.

298
30:05.800 --> 30:05.840
Thank you for tucking Mademoiselle in.

299
30:05.840 --> 30:10.200
Thank you for tucking Mademoiselle in.

300
30:15.880 --> 30:16.880
But it’s not that late yet.

301
30:18.640 --> 30:22.120
But you have to drive home. I’m worried.

302
30:24.040 --> 30:24.680
Get home safe.

303
30:48.960 --> 30:49.640
I’m sorry.

304
30:50.520 --> 30:51.960
I’ll be leaving now.

305
31:04.040 --> 31:04.600
Pun.

306
31:05.800 --> 31:06.560
You just…

307
31:07.560 --> 31:08.160
Forget it.

308
31:08.600 --> 31:09.240
No, no.

309
31:10.000 --> 31:10.760
I mean…

310
31:12.040 --> 31:15.560
I didn’t think you were ready for this.

311
31:19.840 --> 31:22.560
Then why do you think I followed you home today?

312
31:25.200 --> 31:27.280
I thought you wanted to play with my dog.

313
31:33.000 --> 31:34.200
Do you think it’s too soon?

314
31:38.080 --> 31:38.480
I…

315
31:40.920 --> 31:41.160
Yes.

316
31:44.720 --> 31:47.080
But I don’t mind, though.

317
31:51.040 --> 31:52.000
I don’t either.

318
32:37.920 --> 32:38.360
Hi, Dean.

319
32:38.400 --> 32:40.880
Hey! You’re not late at all. Everyone’s leaving.

320
32:41.200 --> 32:41.960
But you’re still here, aren’t you?

321
32:42.040 --> 32:42.560
Right.

322
32:43.200 --> 32:45.200
Whoa!

323
32:47.760 --> 32:48.680
Take it easy.

324
33:09.160 --> 33:09.960
Whoo!

325
33:12.320 --> 33:13.360
What did I do wrong?

326
33:13.560 --> 33:14.800
How is he better than me?

327
33:14.920 --> 33:17.760
♪ My heart feels numb ♪

328
33:19.280 --> 33:20.680
A rocker has possessed him.

329
33:20.920 --> 33:22.680
Shit! What did I do?

330
33:22.880 --> 33:23.880
I got it bad.

331
34:06.840 --> 34:07.600
A bottle of beer.

332
34:55.360 --> 34:55.960
Hey, Moth.

333
34:58.480 --> 34:59.840
Why didn’t you call when you got here?

334
35:03.440 --> 35:04.200
So, what do you think?

335
35:04.560 --> 35:06.680
Seeing my work now, don’t you have anything to say?

336
35:07.640 --> 35:08.440
Go ahead and slam it.

337
35:09.840 --> 35:10.440
Are you crazy?

338
35:12.440 --> 35:13.440
Why would I slam your work?

339
35:16.200 --> 35:19.680
As if I could ever paint something like this.

340
35:20.040 --> 35:20.640
Of course you could.

341
35:21.880 --> 35:23.320
You absolutely could.

342
35:30.320 --> 35:32.000
Your colors are still as precise as ever.

343
35:33.560 --> 35:33.880
No.

344
35:34.680 --> 35:35.480
They’re even more precise than before.

345
35:39.720 --> 35:40.720
You were good before.

346
35:42.600 --> 35:43.880
And now, you’re even better.

347
35:45.280 --> 35:49.120
I guess that’s what an artist is supposed to be.

348
35:49.680 --> 35:51.360
I just paint the way my feelings tell me to.

349
35:52.160 --> 35:53.200
Just like you.

350
35:56.760 --> 35:59.760
When I work, all I think about are deadlines.

351
36:00.480 --> 36:01.360
Will I finish on time?

352
36:02.280 --> 36:03.600
If I do it this way, will the client ask me to change it?

353
36:05.720 --> 36:07.200
Will people like my drawing style?

354
36:08.400 --> 36:09.320
What’s trending these days?

355
36:10.600 --> 36:14.320
But in the end, it all comes down to how you feel, doesn’t it?

356
36:20.040 --> 36:20.520
No.

357
36:26.240 --> 36:30.480
When I work, I haven’t felt anything for a long time.

358
36:39.360 --> 36:40.400
Then that’s a shame.

359
36:41.720 --> 36:44.480
Because that’s exactly your charm.

360
36:51.200 --> 36:55.160
But I think I can still see it in you.

361
36:59.600 --> 37:00.120
What do you see?

362
37:01.760 --> 37:02.600
Please. Don’t say something ridiculous.

363
37:03.120 --> 37:04.360
Hey, Moth.

364
37:06.280 --> 37:08.120
You still think you’re ordinary, don’t you?

365
37:11.200 --> 37:12.040
But to me,

366
37:17.520 --> 37:18.600
you’re the most special person there is.

367
37:26.240 --> 37:27.640
Walk around and take a look.

368
37:28.520 --> 37:29.440
I have to do a photoshoot with the press.

369
37:30.600 --> 37:31.160
I’ll be right back.

370
37:33.560 --> 37:33.840
Sure.

371
37:47.520 --> 37:48.440
(Don’t ever think you’re ordinary.)

372
37:50.960 --> 37:51.840
(Promise me, Moth.)

373
37:53.160 --> 37:54.720
(Don’t ever let that disappear.)

374
37:56.880 --> 37:58.280
(I’d love to keep seeing it.)

375
38:16.400 --> 38:17.280
Did you follow me?

376
38:21.320 --> 38:23.040
Yeah. I did.

377
38:23.920 --> 38:27.000
I wanted to see how many times one person can turn into a lovesick dog.

378
38:28.760 --> 38:29.360
How funny.

379
38:30.080 --> 38:31.800
You’ve spent all these years heartbroken,

380
38:33.160 --> 38:34.280
yet the moment he says something nice to you,

381
38:35.160 --> 38:36.600
you’re grinning from ear to ear.

382
38:37.880 --> 38:38.840
Are you really that happy?

383
38:44.200 --> 38:44.680
Are you drunk?

384
38:46.080 --> 38:46.760
Drunk? No.

385
38:47.160 --> 38:49.280
If you’re not drunk, then what are you?

386
38:54.160 --> 38:54.560
Jealous?

387
38:58.480 --> 38:59.680
Jealous of what? Huh?

388
39:00.440 --> 39:01.120
Why would I be?

389
39:02.000 --> 39:02.800
We’re friends.

390
39:05.360 --> 39:06.080
Am I even allowed?

391
39:11.640 --> 39:12.160
Hey.

392
39:14.680 --> 39:15.600
Is he the friend I met that day?

393
39:17.600 --> 39:18.320
I guess so.

394
39:19.560 --> 39:20.520
Just like Moth said.

395
39:21.760 --> 39:22.560
I’m just a friend.

396
39:25.360 --> 39:28.080
I’m glad you came to see my exhibition.

397
39:34.240 --> 39:35.360
You graduated overseas, right?

398
39:36.120 --> 39:39.360
Should I greet you the Thai way, or should we shake hands?

399
39:42.440 --> 39:44.160
Can I get a selfie, please?

400
39:44.280 --> 39:46.200
I’d like to brag that I know someone famous.

401
39:55.080 --> 39:55.680
Whoo!

402
39:58.240 --> 40:01.680
I just followed you. Don’t forget to follow me back.

403
40:05.840 --> 40:08.120
Mes, I’ll take my friend home.

404
40:10.280 --> 40:10.720
Moth.

405
40:13.920 --> 40:15.280
There’s a party tonight.

406
40:16.160 --> 40:19.080
I want to introduce you to someone.

407
40:21.040 --> 40:22.760
You can bring your friend along.

408
40:28.080 --> 40:30.560
I’m not sure if I can stay until then.

409
40:30.760 --> 40:31.360
But I can.

410
40:33.880 --> 40:36.160
I’ll see you tonight, Mes.

411
40:36.920 --> 40:37.280
Come here.

412
40:48.760 --> 40:49.800
Stop acting crazy and go home.

413
40:50.120 --> 40:50.880
Why do you have to yell?

414
40:52.400 --> 40:54.520
Do you even realize what you’re doing?

415
40:55.000 --> 40:55.520
I do.

416
40:56.720 --> 40:58.280
I’m getting to know your senior.

417
40:59.120 --> 41:00.000
Isn’t he famous?

418
41:01.160 --> 41:02.720
I want to know a competent artist.

419
41:03.800 --> 41:04.680
Maybe it’ll make me look smarter.

420
41:10.920 --> 41:12.480
Go sleep it off for a night or two.

421
41:14.080 --> 41:15.120
We’ll talk when you’re sober.

422
41:23.000 --> 41:23.440
Okay.

423
41:24.480 --> 41:25.120
I’ll go home.

424
41:26.000 --> 41:29.160
But I’ll see you tonight anyway.

425
41:31.400 --> 41:31.800
No.

426
41:33.000 --> 41:33.520
Don’t come.

427
41:33.640 --> 41:34.000
Why not?

428
41:34.520 --> 41:36.520
Didn’t you hear him? He invited me, too.

429
41:39.080 --> 41:42.560
If you f*cking come, I’ll hate you for the rest of my life.

430
42:02.200 --> 42:03.320
Let me introduce you to Sam.

431
42:05.600 --> 42:08.520
I’ve been following his work since his uni days.

432
42:09.520 --> 42:10.440
Hi, Sam.

433
42:11.080 --> 42:12.760
Oh, hey, Mes.

434
42:12.840 --> 42:15.080
Congratulations. The exhibition was a huge success.

435
42:15.400 --> 42:17.200
Seeing how many people showed up made me jealous.

436
42:17.960 --> 42:18.600
Thank you.

437
42:19.600 --> 42:21.840
Sam, this is Moth.

438
42:22.560 --> 42:23.720
He was my junior in the same faculty.

439
42:24.920 --> 42:27.440
He’s making art, too.

440
42:30.000 --> 42:30.440
Hello.

441
42:30.600 --> 42:31.160
Hello.

442
42:31.840 --> 42:33.200
What kind of artwork do you do?

443
42:33.800 --> 42:36.520
Drawing? Painting? Sculpture?

444
42:37.640 --> 42:38.120
Ah.

445
42:39.680 --> 42:40.800
I’m a character artist.

446
42:46.320 --> 42:48.600
I do graphic design sometimes, too.

447
42:51.640 --> 42:53.440
Oh, that’s interesting.

448
42:56.360 --> 43:00.960
I saw his work. He’s really talented.

449
43:02.680 --> 43:03.080
Hey.

450
43:04.040 --> 43:05.840
Chat and his friends are looking for you.

451
43:06.200 --> 43:07.640
They might have a great project for you.

452
43:07.960 --> 43:08.640
Why don’t we go talk to them?

453
43:08.880 --> 43:09.200
Of course.

454
43:12.600 --> 43:14.400
Moth, I’ll be right back.

455
43:15.680 --> 43:16.120
Sure.

456
43:21.120 --> 43:21.720
Mes is here.

457
43:22.200 --> 43:24.200
I heard you had a good project for him.

458
43:24.680 --> 43:25.240
Hi, Chat.

459
44:06.800 --> 44:08.360
(Go sleep it off for a night or two.)

460
44:10.320 --> 44:11.440
(We’ll talk when you’re sober.)

461
44:18.480 --> 44:19.160
Hey.

462
44:20.080 --> 44:22.880
I think you should just tell him and get it over with.

463
44:26.840 --> 44:28.280
Tell him you like him.

464
44:29.200 --> 44:30.920
Tell him you can’t stand the thought of him leaving.

465
44:40.040 --> 44:40.680
Excuse me for a minute.

466
44:42.840 --> 44:43.120
Moth.

467
44:47.040 --> 44:48.400
I’m going to Chat’s house party afterward.

468
44:49.400 --> 44:49.880
Come with me.

469
44:52.320 --> 44:53.040
It’s okay.

470
44:54.280 --> 44:57.560
You go ahead. I think I’ll head home.

471
44:59.000 --> 44:59.840
What’s the hurry?

472
45:01.880 --> 45:02.640
Do you have plans with someone?

473
45:05.200 --> 45:08.200
I need to finish an illustration. I’m already two days late.

474
45:10.320 --> 45:11.240
You go to the party.

475
45:13.320 --> 45:15.440
I’ll go home and make a living.

476
45:20.560 --> 45:20.960
Moth.

477
45:24.160 --> 45:25.240
Will you paint again?

478
45:30.160 --> 45:31.240
I am painting.

479
45:32.280 --> 45:33.000
No.

480
45:37.040 --> 45:39.920
I’m not talking about those comic characters.

481
45:41.840 --> 45:42.440
I mean…

482
45:49.080 --> 45:51.520
I think you know what I mean.

483
46:10.000 --> 46:10.960
Paint again, Moth.

484
46:14.080 --> 46:16.200
Give me a chance to see your work again.

485
46:25.560 --> 46:28.680
And don’t worry about whether anyone buys it.

486
46:30.520 --> 46:31.400
Because I will.

487
46:33.280 --> 46:35.320
No matter how expensive it is.

488
48:00.480 --> 48:02.800
[MANIAC]

489
48:10.200 --> 48:10.840
(Hey.)

490
48:13.040 --> 48:14.320
(I’m sorry I crossed the line.)

491
48:17.680 --> 48:19.440
I don’t know what got into me.

492
48:21.320 --> 48:22.280
I was a f*cking asshole.

493
48:24.800 --> 48:26.160
If I were you, I’d kick my ass.

494
48:31.640 --> 48:32.400
(I’m sorry.)

495
48:34.040 --> 48:34.760
(I…)

496
48:36.840 --> 48:37.840
Can you not hate me?

497
48:41.640 --> 48:42.640
(Please don’t hate me.)

498
49:06.040 --> 49:06.440
Here.

499
49:54.640 --> 49:57.240
The artist party wasn’t fun?

500
49:59.120 --> 50:00.960
Is that why you came out here to sit by yourself?

501
50:01.600 --> 50:02.440
What’s there to have fun about?

502
50:04.440 --> 50:07.680
Those people don’t know how to have fun.

503
50:10.240 --> 50:11.240
Aren’t you one of those people?

504
50:17.000 --> 50:17.520
Good point.

505
50:20.040 --> 50:20.960
I don’t know.

506
50:23.480 --> 50:27.480
Let’s just say I know what fun is.

507
50:29.320 --> 50:32.320
And being with those people isn’t it.

508
50:34.400 --> 50:35.080
Should we hit a nightclub?

509
50:36.360 --> 50:37.400
Have some crazy fun.

510
50:38.080 --> 50:40.680
No. I’d rather stay here.

511
50:48.040 --> 50:54.800
Have you forgiven me for what happened at the gallery?

512
50:58.160 --> 50:58.800
Don’t talk about it.

513
51:00.440 --> 51:01.080
I don’t want to dig it back up.

514
51:17.480 --> 51:18.560
I want to be a cat.

515
51:22.520 --> 51:23.040
Huh?

516
51:24.160 --> 51:24.960
I want to be a cat.

517
51:27.240 --> 51:30.280
Maybe things will get easier.

518
51:34.320 --> 51:35.120
Are you all right?

519
51:37.600 --> 51:38.080
You okay?

520
51:40.400 --> 51:45.240
Right now, I don’t know if I’m doing something I actually like.

521
51:46.920 --> 51:51.200
I don’t even know who I am anymore.

522
51:58.800 --> 51:59.960
Is there anything I can help you with?

523
52:07.760 --> 52:08.600
Can’t think of anything now.

524
52:11.160 --> 52:12.360
You can tell me when you do.

525
52:16.120 --> 52:16.920
Um…

526
52:22.560 --> 52:23.640
Can I sleep on your lap?

527
52:44.080 --> 52:46.240
Anything else you want?

528
52:48.960 --> 52:49.720
Um…

529
52:54.080 --> 52:55.080
Will you sing for me?

530
52:55.960 --> 52:56.320
What?

531
52:59.760 --> 53:03.280
I’m afraid that’ll just stress you out more.

532
53:05.640 --> 53:06.320
Come on.

533
53:09.080 --> 53:09.920
You’re not going to do it?

534
53:19.600 --> 53:25.880
♪ Stay with me tonight If there’s no one there to hold you ♪

535
53:26.080 --> 53:30.440
♪ Stay with me Until the morning light breaks through ♪

536
53:40.920 --> 53:45.760
“You don’t have to stand your ground on everything. Your legs will get sore.”

537
53:47.040 --> 53:47.800
What are you talking about?

538
53:48.880 --> 53:49.920
Don’t you want to be a cat?

539
53:50.640 --> 53:51.880
Then try thinking like one.

540
54:03.840 --> 54:07.240
“Never say never. Unless you mean ‘never mind.’”

541
54:46.040 --> 54:48.080
There’s an exhibition next week.

542
54:48.960 --> 54:52.160
If you pull this off, you can finally become a full-fledged artist.

543
54:52.480 --> 54:53.200
What should I do?

544
54:53.760 --> 54:58.760
You mean with the art, or with your relationship with Dean?

545
54:59.600 --> 55:01.480
How would you like me to help?

546
55:03.800 --> 55:05.160
Don’t paint so much that you faint. — Dean

547
55:08.280 --> 55:08.880
I miss you.

548
55:09.600 --> 55:10.400
Miss you, too.

549
55:11.320 --> 55:12.320
Your painting is beautiful.

550
55:13.200 --> 55:13.880
So damn beautiful.
